Third-party data
================

Code page tables (internal/codepage/tables.go)
----------------------------------------------

The tables of the single-byte code pages are the content of the mapping
files published by the Unicode Consortium, written out as Go arrays:

  Windows 874, 1250, 1251, 1252, 1253, 1254, 1255, 1256, 1257, 1258:
    https://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/VENDORS/MICSFT/WINDOWS/CP874.TXT
    https://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/VENDORS/MICSFT/WINDOWS/CP1250.TXT
    ... through CP1258.TXT
  Mac OS Roman (code page 10000):
    https://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/VENDORS/APPLE/ROMAN.TXT

The files are provided by the Unicode Consortium and the vendors named in
them (Microsoft Corporation, Apple Inc.) under the Unicode terms of use,
which permit use of the mapping data. Bytes the files leave undefined are
undefined in the tables (decoded as U+FFFD with a warning).

The tables were transcribed while this library was written, without network
access to the files; tables_test.go checks the structure of each table and a
sample of known values. A byte-by-byte comparison with the published files
is recommended before release (see the README, "What is not read").

No other third-party code or data is included. The double-byte code pages
(932, 936, 949, 950) are not decoded, because no table generated from
authoritative content is included.
